police have arrested a man on suspicion  of murder after two young girls aged  three and one were killed in a fire in  Nottingham investigators say the blaze  was started deliberately officers are  appealing for anyone who was in the area  at the time and might have seen  something to come forward Becky Johnson  reports from Nottingham a warning there  are some flashing lights from the start  I just woke up in the early hours of the  morning to see this firefighters trying  to stop the smoke that was billowing  from the first floor flat  people watched in horror as they  realized two children were inside  neighbors they first they saw  firefighters carrying out the  three-year-old girl before an emergency  worker emerged cradling the one-year-old  the children were taken over the road  where paramedics tried to resuscitate  them before they went by ambulance to  hospital  their lives couldn't be saved their  mother who was also rescued from the  flat remains critically ill in hospital  by morning the blackened windows were  the only outward sign of the terror they  must have felt inside on this quiet  street in Clifton in Nottingham people  were told to stay indoors  and then came news that police believed  the fire wasn't an accident  31 year old local man has been arrested  on suspicion of murder and attempted  murder he remains in custody  the fire took hold of the first floor of  the property and neighboring properties  were evacuated two children were treated  at the scene for smoke inhalation but  unfortunately despite bester efforts  they passed away at hospital this  morning a woman also within the property  was taken to Queen's Medical Center  where she remains in a critical  condition  forensic investigations will likely take  some time officers have taken away  potential evidence for examination  Sadness the loss of life compounded by  shock that someone could have done this  deliberately  Becky Johnson Sky News Nottingham
 

